 "name": "129-space-groups",
 "description": "On a line that holds a tab, a number token can group its digits in threes with one space, no-break space, thin space or narrow no-break space between the groups, as in '36 428 426'. A tab ends the token, so two cells never join. On a line with no tab, two spaces, or a group of other than 3 digits, the space ends the token as before. A span that starts inside a grouped token reads no value, and a candidate value never uses space groups. A number character other than 0 to 9 after the match, and the 000 of a currency scale at its start, make no grouped token (spec 0.12, #427).",
